argin could tighten considerably.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jim Pillen (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Nebraska's governor's race pits incumbent Republican Jim Pillen against Democrat Lynne Walz, with two independents also on the ballot. The state leans about ten points Republican, and Pillen holds the advantages of incumbency in a midterm environment that has leaned somewhat against the party in power. Five of seven expert raters call the race Solid Republican, with two saying Likely Republican.\n\nPolling since early September shows Pillen ahead in every survey, though margins range from a tie in a Democratic-sponsored poll to a seventeen-point Republican lead. Averaging recent surveys puts Pillen up roughly six to eight points, and prediction markets give Walz between three and ten percent. Pillen has campaigned with President Trump and earned an NRA endorsement, while the Farm Bureau stayed neutral after backing him in 2022. Walz is on the air and courting cross-party support, but the evidence points to a clear Republican favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -11.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0639, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0714, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0694, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0605, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0982, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0987, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0922, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -8.5}]}